cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use BioTransport in work you publish, please cite it.
title: "BioTransport: a science-first transport solver for teaching and prototyping"
abstract: >-
  BioTransport solves diffusion, advection and reaction problems on structured
  meshes with a C++17 finite-volume core and a Python API. It is built around
  verification: it ships the exact solutions to compare numerical results
  against, reports the dimensionless groups that govern a configured problem,
  records what each solver claims and excludes, and refuses configurations it
  cannot certify rather than returning an unverified answer.
type: software
